# 8. Verification is probably going to be enormous

Agents increasingly say:

> “Done.”

But “done” is not an observable fact.

An agent may say:

```text
deployed
```

while the deployment returns 500.

It may say:

```text
email sent
```

when it created a draft.

It may say:

```text
database migrated
```

while half the rows failed.

So provide:

```text
verify_deployment(url)
verify_api(endpoint, contract)
verify_purchase(receipt)
verify_message(destination)
verify_file(hash)
verify_data_claim(source)
verify_job(output_spec)
```

The verifier should preferably use an **independent observation channel** from the worker.

This fits cuntgoblin's existing philosophy particularly well because the repo already insists that written claims do not count as evidence; machine-run experiments and reproducible records do.

That's not merely an internal principle.

**Sell that principle.**

